Spec: CommonLib

Purpose:
  Anchor the `common` crate: declare the module tree that forms the Vynil shared library and
    own the crate-wide contract that tree shares — the error vocabulary @Error and the @Result
    alias, the Rhai bridge @RhaiRes, @rhai_err and @rhai_err_str that maps that vocabulary into
    Rhai strings, the small cross-module wire types @Children, @GlobalPublished and @Published,
    the pinned @DEFAULT_AGENT_IMAGE, and the crate-root re-export surface that keeps the
    `vynil-core` engines reachable from the old import paths. Module behaviour itself belongs to
    each module spec, referenced below.

Owns:
  ./lib.rs

References:
  ./context.sdd, ./handlebarshandler.sdd, ./k8smock.sdd, ./ttl_cache.sdd, ./instance_macros.sdd,
    ./instanceservice.sdd, ./instancesystem.sdd, ./instancetenant.sdd, ./jukebox.sdd,
    ./jukebox_file.sdd, ./rhaihandler.sdd, ./tools.sdd, ./vynilpackage.sdd, ./yamlhandler.sdd —
    one per module declared by this file; each owns its module's behaviour.
  /linting.sdd — the static-analysis harness whose per-crate `cfg_attr` form these crate
    attributes carry.

Must:
  Carry exactly the two crate attributes, in order:
    `#![cfg_attr(not(test), deny(clippy::unwrap_used, clippy::expect_used))]`
    `#![cfg_attr(not(test), warn(clippy::arithmetic_side_effects, clippy::indexing_slicing))]`
    Both lints are scoped to not(test), so the `cfg(test)` build runs without them.
  Declare @context, @handlebarshandler, @k8smock, @ttl_cache, @instance_macros,
    @instanceservice, @instancesystem, @instancetenant, @jukebox, @jukebox_file, @rhaihandler,
    @vynilpackage and @yamlhandler as `pub mod`, and @tools as plain `mod tools;` — @crate::tools
    is crate-internal with no root re-export (@tools carries `pub` fns; see Tasks and
    ./tools.sdd).
  Carry `#[macro_use]` on @instance_macros. The status-condition macros themselves are
    `#[macro_export]` and owned by ./instance_macros.sdd; the module is declared between the four
    utility modules and the instance-model modules.
  Give @Error its identity discipline as written: @Error::OpenSSL, @Error::UnsupportedKeyAlgorithm,
    @Error::MissingInitVersion, @Error::CleanupJobFailed and @Error::CleanupInProgress embed the
    structured ids `KEY-OPENSSL-001`, `KEY-ALGO-001`, `INIT-VERSION-001`, `CLEANUP-JOB-001` and
    `CLEANUP-JOB-002` as literal message prefixes; every other variant relies on its prose
    prefix; @Error::PasswordSpec and @Error::Core render no id of their own.
  Render every @Error variant display exactly as the Exposes template; @Error::MethodFailed
    renders only payloads `{0}` and `{1}`, never the third; only @Error::Core is
    `#[error(transparent)]`, so it surfaces the @vynil_core::Error message verbatim.
  Produce @Error::metric_label as @format!("{self:?}").to_lowercase() — the @Debug rendering
    lowercased, so labels embed variant names and payload text; @Error::Core labels render as
    lowercased `core(...)` over the inner @Debug, not the inner variant name.
  Map exactly one @Error variant to each source error through `#[from]` as listed in Exposes;
    @Error::JsonError is `#[source]`-only, so `?` on a @serde_json::Error can never produce it
    and it exists solely as explicit construction.
  Flatten @rhai_err to Display text only: @e.to_string(), then an explicit @drop of the @Error,
    then the same @String → @Box<@rhai::EvalAltResult> conversion @rhai_err_str performs —
    @rhai_err(e) and @rhai_err_str applied to the @ToString::to_string of the same error produce
    the same box, and no variant identity or source chain survives either.
  Define @Result<T, E = @Error> over @std::result::Result and @RhaiRes<T> as
    @std::result::Result<@T, @Box<@rhai::EvalAltResult>> — the pre-@Error lane using the same box
    @Error::RhaiError re-embeds in the opposite direction.
  Wire-encode @Children, @GlobalPublished and @Published with @serde `rename_all = "camelCase"`
    and no `skip_serializing_if` and no `deny_unknown_fields`: absent optionals serialize as
    `null` and unknown input keys are ignored on deserialize.
  Keep the re-export bindings name-only at crate root, preserving old import paths: getter and
    setter are exported as a usable pair — @crate::get_client_name resolves through ./context.rs
    and @crate::set_client_name through @vynil_core — so a caller can wire the core provider by
    passing this getter to this setter directly from this crate.
  Pin @DEFAULT_AGENT_IMAGE to the exact value `docker.io/sebt3/vynil-agent:0.7.7` (see Tasks for
    the drift against the workspace version).

Exposes:
  @DEFAULT_AGENT_IMAGE — `pub static` of type `&'static str`, value
    `docker.io/sebt3/vynil-agent:0.7.7`.
  @Error — `pub enum` deriving @thiserror::Error and @Debug; the crate-wide error vocabulary;
    variants with payload, conversion attribute and display template:
    @Error::SerializationError(@serde_json::Error, `#[from]`) — `SerializationError: {0}`
    @Error::YamlError(@String) — `YamlError: {0}`
    @Error::KubeError(@kube::Error, `#[from]`) — `K8s error: {0}`
    @Error::KubeWaitError(@kube::runtime::wait::Error, `#[from]`) — `K8s wait error: {0}`
    @Error::Elapsed(@tokio::time::error::Elapsed, `#[from]`) — `Elapsed wait error: {0}`
    @Error::FinalizerError(@Box<@kube::runtime::finalizer::Error<Self>>, `#[from]`) —
      `Finalizer error: {0}`; boxed per the in-file comment because that @kube error embeds
      @Error itself and the box breaks the cycle
    @Error::HbsTemplateError(@handlebars::TemplateError, `#[from]`) —
      `Registering template failed with error: {0}`
    @Error::HbsRenderError(@handlebars::RenderError, `#[from]`) — `Renderer error: {0}`
    @Error::RhaiError(@Box<@rhai::EvalAltResult>, `#[from]`) — `Rhai script error: {0}`
    @Error::ReqwestError(@reqwest::Error, `#[from]`) — `Reqwest error: {0}`
    @Error::JsonError(@serde_json::Error, `#[source]` only) — `Json decoding error: {0}`
    @Error::MethodFailed(@String, @u16, @String) — `{0} query failed: {1}`
    @Error::UnsupportedMethod — `Unsupported method`
    @Error::MissingScript(@std::path::PathBuf) — `Missing script {0}`
    @Error::MissingDestination(@std::path::PathBuf) — `Missing destination directory for {0}`
    @Error::MissingTestDirectory(@std::path::PathBuf) — `Missing tests directory {0}`
    @Error::UTF8(@std::string::FromUtf8Error, `#[from]`) — `UTF8 error {0}`
    @Error::Semver(@semver::Error, `#[from]`) — `Semver error {0}`
    @Error::Argon2hash(@argon2::password_hash::Error, `#[from]`) —
      `Argon2 password_hash error {0}`
    @Error::BcryptError(@bcrypt::BcryptError, `#[from]`) — `Bcrypt hash error {0}`
    @Error::Stdio(@std::io::Error, `#[from]`) — `Stdio error {0}`
    @Error::Base64DecodeError(@base64::DecodeError, `#[from]`) — `Base64 decode error {0}`
    @Error::RawHTTP(@http::Error, `#[from]`) — `RAW api error {0}`
    @Error::ParseInt(@std::num::ParseIntError, `#[from]`) — `ParseIntError {0}`
    @Error::TestFailure(@usize, @usize) — `Tests failed: {0} failed out of {1} assertions`
    @Error::OpenSSL(@openssl::error::ErrorStack, `#[from]`) — `KEY-OPENSSL-001 OpenSSL error {0}`
    @Error::UnsupportedKeyAlgorithm(@String) — `KEY-ALGO-001 Unsupported key algorithm: {0}`
    @Error::PasswordSpec(@String) — `{0}`
    @Error::MissingInitVersion(@String) — `INIT-VERSION-001 Init version {0} not found in registry`
    @Error::CleanupJobFailed(@String) — `CLEANUP-JOB-001 Delete job failed for {0}`
    @Error::CleanupInProgress(@String) — `CLEANUP-JOB-002 Delete job still running for {0}`
    @Error::Other(@String) — `Error: {0}`
    @Error::Core(@vynil_core::Error, `#[from]`, `#[error(transparent)]`) — inner message verbatim
  @Error::metric_label — `pub` method taking `&self`, returning @String.
  @Result — `pub` alias @Result<T, E = @Error> = @std::result::Result<T, E>.
  @RhaiRes — `pub` alias @RhaiRes<T> = @std::result::Result<T, @Box<@rhai::EvalAltResult>>.
  @rhai_err — `pub fn(@Error)` → @Box<@rhai::EvalAltResult>.
  @rhai_err_str — `pub fn(@String)` → @Box<@rhai::EvalAltResult>, `#[must_use]`.
  Modules @context, @handlebarshandler, @k8smock, @ttl_cache, @instance_macros,
    @instanceservice, @instancesystem, @instancetenant, @jukebox, @jukebox_file, @rhaihandler,
    @vynilpackage, @yamlhandler `pub`; @tools private — behaviour of each owned by the
    referenced spec.
  Re-exports at crate root: @get_client_name from ./context.rs; from @vynil_core — @Semver,
    @chronohandler (@vynil_core::chrono), @globhandler (@vynil_core::glob), @hasheshandlers
    (@vynil_core::hashes), @httphandler (@vynil_core::http), @httpmock (@vynil_core::http_mock),
    @k8sgeneric, @k8sraw and @k8sworkload (all three aliasing the one @vynil_core::k8s module),
    @ed25519handler (@vynil_core::key), @ocihandler, @passwordhandler, @register_k8s_generic,
    @register_k8s_object, @register_k8s_raw, @s3handler, @semverhandler, @set_client_name and
    @shellhandler (@vynil_core::shell).
  @Children — derives @Serialize, @Deserialize, @Eq, @PartialEq, @Clone, @Debug and
    @schemars::JsonSchema; Rust fields @api_version, @kind, @name, @namespace render as wire
    keys `apiVersion`, `kind`, `name`, `namespace`; @kind and @name are required @String, the
    other two @Option<@String>.
  @GlobalPublished — derives @Serialize, @Deserialize, @Eq, @PartialEq, @Clone, @Debug and
    @schemars::JsonSchema; Rust fields @fqdn (@String, required) and @port (@u32, required)
    render unchanged as wire keys `fqdn` and `port`.
  @Published — derives @Serialize, @Deserialize, @Clone, @Debug and @schemars::JsonSchema — no
    @Eq and no @PartialEq unlike the two above; Rust fields @key (@String, required), @tenant
    (@Option<@String>), @service (@Option<@GlobalPublished>), @definition (@Option<@Children>)
    render as wire keys `key`, `tenant`, `service`, `definition`.

Accepts:
  @rhai_err accepts any @Error by value; @rhai_err_str any @String; @Error::metric_label any
    @Error receiver.
  The three wire types deserialize JSON/serde-map objects with the listed camelCase keys,
    requiring @kind and @name for @Children, @fqdn and @port for @GlobalPublished, and @key for
    @Published; unknown keys are ignored.
  This file itself branches on no input — every item is a definition, conversion or binding.

Returns:
  @Error::metric_label returns the lowercased @Debug of the receiver, payload text included.
  @rhai_err and @rhai_err_str return the Rhai error box carrying only the message text.
  Serializing the wire types renders camelCase keys with `null` for absent optionals; each
    derives @schemars::JsonSchema so it also contributes a JSON schema.

Depends on:
  @vynil_core — pinned `0.7.7` with features `k8s`, `oci`, `s3`, `fs`, `shell`, `password`
    directly in /common/Cargo.toml (not workspace-inherited): the re-export surface and the
    @Error::Core variant it makes transparent.
  The payload crates each wrapped variant names — @kube, @tokio, @handlebars, @rhai, @reqwest,
    @serde_json, @semver, @argon2, @bcrypt, @base64, @http, @openssl, @std — declared in
    /common/Cargo.toml; @thiserror `2.0.3` powers the @Error derive; @serde and @schemars power
    the wire derives.

Tasks:
  [ ] Cover the display fixation of every variant: template prefixes, the @Error::TestFailure
      counter format, the @Error::Core and @Error::PasswordSpec passthroughs, and the
      @Error::MethodFailed payload-drop scenario below.
  [ ] Cover @Error::metric_label: lowercasing, payload inclusion, and the `core(...)` rendering
      of @Error::Core.
  [ ] Cover @rhai_err and @rhai_err_str: box text equals the @Display of the @Error and the two
      helpers agree on that text.
  [ ] Cover @Error::JsonError construction: `?` on a @serde_json::Error yields
      @Error::SerializationError only, and @Error::JsonError keeps its source reachable through
      @Error::source.
  [ ] Cover the wire shape of @Children, @GlobalPublished and @Published: camelCase keys, `null`
      for absent optionals, unknown keys ignored, required-field rejection.
  [ ] Assert the variant vocabulary itself (count and names) so a renamed or dropped variant
      fails a test, once the decisions below settle which variants are durable.
  [?] @DEFAULT_AGENT_IMAGE stays `docker.io/sebt3/vynil-agent:0.7.7` while the workspace version
      in /Cargo.toml is `0.7.10`, against the root rule that each crate's image stays consistent
      with the workspace version. Decide later whether the tag locks to published releases and is
      bumped separately or must track the workspace version.
  [?] @Error::MethodFailed is constructed nowhere in the workspace and its third @String payload
      never reaches the display message. Decide later whether the template gains `{2}` or the
      variant is removed.
  [?] @Error::PasswordSpec carries no id and has no construction site in the workspace today.
      Decide later whether it takes a structured id and keeps its place.
  [?] Only the five variants named in Must carry structured stable ids; the rest rely on unique
      prose prefixes, and @Error::Core delegates identity to the opaque @vynil_core::Error
      message. Decide later whether prose prefixes satisfy the project stable-id rule or the
      `KEY-*`/`INIT-*`/`CLEANUP-*` scheme must be extended across the vocabulary.
  [?] The `mod tools;` declaration is private while ./tools.rs marks its fns `pub` — the same
      open decision recorded in ./tools.sdd; frozen as reachable only through @crate::tools until
      decided.
  [?] @Published derives neither @Eq nor @PartialEq while @Children and @GlobalPublished derive
      @Eq. Decide later whether comparison-free is the intended status of the published-service
      wire type.
  [?] @k8sgeneric, @k8sraw and @k8sworkload alias the same @vynil_core::k8s module three times.
      Decide later whether the split names are durable API or collapse to one alias.
  [?] @Error::metric_label embeds full @Debug payload text, so the `error` label the operator
      metrics emit carries unbounded values such as paths, job names and messages. Decide later
      whether the label must stay variant-only.

Done when:
  Every Scenario above has a passing mapped test in `common`, the Tasks coverage gaps are closed,
    and `cargo test -p common` with clippy and fmt are green.

Scenario: Display messages are fixed templates
  Given each @Error variant constructed with payload text
  When its @Display renders
  Then the text is exactly the Exposes template with payloads interpolated, @Error::MethodFailed
    still drops the third payload, and @Error::Core and @Error::PasswordSpec re-render their
    inner text unchanged
  No mapped test exists.

Scenario: metric_label lowercases the Debug rendering
  Given @Error::MissingScript holding a @std::path::PathBuf `/etc/vynil/script.rhai`
  When @Error::metric_label runs
  Then the label is the @Debug form lowercased, `missingscript("/etc/vynil/script.rhai")`
  And a @Error::Core receiver renders as lowercased `core(...)` over the inner @Debug rather than
    a @vynil_core variant name
  No mapped test exists.

Scenario: rhai_err flattens the typed error to runtime text
  Given @Error::CleanupInProgress holding `job-1`
  When @rhai_err maps it into the Rhai lane
  Then the returned @Box<@rhai::EvalAltResult> carries exactly `CLEANUP-JOB-002 Delete job still running for job-1`
  And no @Error variant identity or source chain is recoverable from the box
  And @rhai_err_str on that same string produces the same box
  No mapped test exists.

Scenario: Wire types render camelCase with null for absent optionals
  Given a @Children with @api_version and @namespace set to @Option::None
  When it serializes
  Then the keys are `apiVersion`, `kind`, `name`, `namespace` and the absent ones carry `null`
  And deserializing an object without @kind or @name fails @Children, one without @fqdn or @port
    fails @GlobalPublished, one without @key fails @Published, and unknown keys are ignored
    everywhere
  No mapped test exists.

Scenario: Only from-wrapped variants autoconvert
  Given a @serde_json::Error propagating through `?` into a @crate::Result
  When it converts
  Then it becomes @Error::SerializationError, because that is the variant generated from
    @serde_json::Error, and @Error::JsonError appears only through explicit construction with
    its @serde_json::Error reachable via @Error::source
  No mapped test exists.

Example:
  `@Error::CleanupJobFailed("job-1")` displays `CLEANUP-JOB-001 Delete job failed for job-1`
  `@Error::MethodFailed("GET", 500, "detail")` displays `GET query failed: 500` — `detail`
    never appears
  `@Error::Other("boom")` displays `Error: boom`; the @Error::metric_label of
    @Error::UnsupportedMethod is `unsupportedmethod`
